                                                    "patching_rect": [ 6.0, 67.0, 315.0, 261.0 ],
                                                    "text": "always use a camera with a fixed exposure!!!\nand look at a space where the light situation does NOT change (no open air sry)\n\nsnap a picture of an empty space (with the button above the snippet)\n\nchanges in pixels will be shown as white pixels\n\nin this way you can recognize if there are people or new objects in the space\n\noutput 1 gives a float measuring the overall brightness (amount of new things present in the picture)\n\noutput 2 gives a greyscale \"un-thresholded\" image\n\noutput 3 gives the B/W image \n(the one previewed)"
